From: devvm <https://github.com/bindreams/devvm>
Subject: [PATCH] target/i386/whpx: guard the optional WHvResetPartition

QEMU loads WHvResetPartition as an optional export
(LIST_WINHVPLATFORM_FUNCTIONS_SUPPLEMENTAL). It is missing on Windows 10, so
the pointer is NULL there and the unconditional call in 0001 crashes QEMU on
guest reset. Skip the call and report instead.

devvm-only; applies after 0001.
---
--- a/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c
+++ b/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c
@@ -530,9 +530,15 @@
 
     /* Assumes that cpu_synchronize_all_post_reset() runs cpu 0 first. */
     if (level == WHPX_LEVEL_RESET_STATE && cpu->cpu_index == 0) {
-        hr = whp_dispatch.WHvResetPartition(whpx->partition);
-        if (FAILED(hr)) {
-            error_report("WHPX: Failed to reset partition, hr=%08lx", hr);
+        /* Optional export: absent before Windows 11. */
+        if (!whp_dispatch.WHvResetPartition) {
+            error_report("WHPX: guest reset needs WHvResetPartition, "
+                         "available on Windows 11 and later");
+        } else {
+            hr = whp_dispatch.WHvResetPartition(whpx->partition);
+            if (FAILED(hr)) {
+                error_report("WHPX: Failed to reset partition, hr=%08lx", hr);
+            }
         }
     }
 
